    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras face a high-upside slate today, headlined by **Junior Caminero**, who commands an elite score of 81.38. His matchup against the favorable 5.06 xERA of J. Lopez is the highlight of the day; the combination of a +10% park factor and the premium protection of the #3 spot in the batting order makes him our undisputed cornerstone. **Yordan Alvarez** remains a must-start at 69.47, as his xwOBA of .467 provides the highest ceiling in the lineup despite a slight park penalty, while **Carson Benge** (61.23) and **Caleb Durbin** (60.77) offer high-floor utility. We are leaning heavily on favorable platoon splits today, particularly with **Carson Benge** and **Christian Yelich**, who both see double-digit boosts in their dynamic platoon projections against right-handed pitching.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Christian Yelich** (58.30) and **Lars Nootbaar** (54.56). While **Christian Yelich** ultimately secured the starting nod due to a superior dynamic platoon advantage (+13%), his score remains volatile given the downward pressure of the #7 batting position and a neutral matchup against Mize. We are closely monitoring the status of the rest of our bench, including **Trea Turner**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, and **Colt Keith**; all are currently excluded due to rest or scheduling gaps, leaving us with limited depth should the late-afternoon lineups shift. **Josh Smith** is currently in the lineup but remains the most \"marginal\" play at 49.38 due to his position at the bottom of the order, which mitigates his favorable platoon edge. No significant weather hazards are currently flagged, but with **Kyle Schwarber** (60.77) leading off, his performance against Dobbins will set the tone for whether we can maximize our run production in a high-leverage 5x5 Roto environment.",
